    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-072 — Regression tests for ADR-071 fixes.** Three unit tests that fail if the ADR-071 fixes are reverted. Without these, the two bugs we spent hours chasing (Wikipedia headings invisible, blank page on scroll) could silently return during future refactors of `layout_block_children` or `paint_children`.\n\n## The 3 tests\n\n| File | Test | Guards |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_layout.cpp` | inline `<h2>` becomes `InlineContext`, not `Box` | Inline-routing fix (ADR-071 §1) |\n| `test_paint.cpp` | `Box` with `h=641` containing descendants at `y=1500` is **not** culled by its own height | Leaf-only culling rule (ADR-071 §3) — reproduces the `<body>`=641px / content=30440px Wikipedia case |\n| `test_paint.cpp` | `Text` leaf far outside visible range **is** still culled | Perf property — a refactor that disables culling entirely would fail this |\n\n## Suite delta\n\n- Test cases: **691 → 694** (+3)\n- Assertions: **2641 → 2646** (+5)\n- Runtime: unchanged (tests are sub-millisecond)\n- All green\n\n## Why this matters\n\nBoth ADR-071 bugs were invisible at fixture scale. They required Wikipedia's specific DOM structure (inline headings inside divs, containers with height ≠ children height) to surface. If they recur, we'd have to re-run the full debugging session to notice — unless a test catches it first.\n\nThe 3 tests are that catch-net. Each is 15–25 lines, exercises a specific structural property, and would fail on the exact commit that reverted the corresponding ADR-071 change.\n\n## What this does NOT test (documented in ADR spec)\n\n- **Wikipedia-scale integration.** Network I/O, real CSS from MediaWiki, real GTK window. Manual visual verification remains the primary gate.\n- **Async logger timing.** Covered by `test_log.cpp` (passes after the dual-mode fix).\n- **Cascade CSS variable resolution.** Wikipedia's `:is()`, `:where()`, `var()` — not exercised headlessly.\n\n## The right pattern going forward\n\nEvery Wikipedia-specific bug fixed gets:\n1. A **structural unit test** if possible (like these three)\n2. A **screenshot-based manual verification** recorded in the ADR\n3. Honest documentation of what couldn't be automated\n\nADR-071 + ADR-072 are the first instance of this pattern. Future ADRs follow it.\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Structural-regression, headless-verified.** Suite green, 3 new tests assert the exact structural properties ADR-071 introduced.\n\nRefs #278\n",
